NMU standalone control/data/random patterns

First run (compile + simulate): make run CASE=ctrl_write_burst
After compilation (reuse binary): make sim CASE=ctrl_write_burst
Shared scenarios (5-12): MODE=control|data|rand, default control
Random example: make sim CASE=same_id_outstanding MODE=rand SEED=7
Fixed ctrl_*/data_* cases select their own mode; request_rand mixes both.
Full matrix: make regress
Waveform: make run_wave CASE=ctrl_write_burst
Display this list: make list

 1. ctrl_write_single
    Single control write
 2. ctrl_read_single
    Single control read
 3. ctrl_write_burst
    Control write bursts: SIZE, FIXED/INCR/WRAP, WSTRB, LAST
 4. ctrl_read_burst
    Control read bursts: SIZE, FIXED/INCR/WRAP, lanes, LAST
 5. same_id_in_order
    Same ID, requests and responses in order
 6. same_id_outstanding
    Same ID, multiple outstanding transactions
 7. multi_id_outstanding
    Multiple IDs and outstanding transactions
 8. cross_id_out_of_order
    Out-of-order responses across IDs
 9. same_id_cross_dst_reorder
    Same ID across destinations, B/R reordering
10. outstanding_full_recover
    Capacity pressure and recovery, including ID remap reuse
11. backpressure
    REQ and AXI response stalls
12. reset_inflight
    Coordinated reset with transactions in flight
13. data_write_single
    Single data write
14. data_write_burst
    Data write bursts: SIZE, FIXED/INCR/WRAP, WSTRB, LAST
15. data_read_single
    Single data read
16. data_read_burst
    Data read bursts: full data bus, beat count, LAST
17. ctrl_rand
    Seeded control requests
18. data_rand
    Seeded data requests
19. request_rand
    Seeded mixed control/data requests

Default simulator: VCS. Local override: SIMULATOR=verilator.
AW/W/AR use the original axi_file_master.run(); no TB outstanding cap.
Changing CASE reuses the binary. Changing DUT settings or WAVE may need compilation.
Pattern ID width must match the compiled DUT.
Legacy traffic patterns: neighbor, uniform_random, hotspot, directed.
Run legacy suite: make legacy_regress
